    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d642">

                <pb facs="0507" n="499" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.115 Panay/46: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief of the United States Asiatic
                        Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Yarnell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Chief of Naval Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leahy</hi>)<anchor n="78" xml:id="d642-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>U. S. S. “<hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Oahu</hi></placeName>,” <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1937-12-14T14:10:00">December 14, 1937—2:10
                            p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 14—9:07 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>0014. Your 0514. 1235. As nearly as can be ascertained <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Panay</hi> capsized and sunk directly abreast lower entrance Hohsien
                    channel about 500 yards from left bank 7 fathoms water, nothing showing; bombed
                    about 1330, sank about 1430, more details upon contact with surviving
                    officers.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
